g were you married may i ask i  was married for 11 years and kind of  still right  because you know the the divorce is  still pending  i'm in limbo and so i am still married  but i was together with my ex for about  11 years  and how long has it been since you've  been separated  about three about three maybe going into  four  because my youngest daughter is four  years old so um  yeah since then and where divorce papers  aside  where do you feel like you're at in the  journey do you still feel like  everything  is as raw and fresh as if it was  yesterday or do you feel like the ship  is leaving the dock a little bit  the ship has almost left the dock i  can't say that i'm a hundred percent  there  but i certainly do not feel the same way  as i did  a few years back so time does heal  and i'm happy that i'm here now i'm so  glad to hear you say that because  everybody said that to me time  i think the way you described it was  really good and it  it i think what nobody talks about is  that it's going to take  probably a lot more time than you really  want it to or anticipate  yes it does take a little bit longer  because we  are as mothers we have that connection  with their fathers so  we can't really say it's out of sight  out of mind we still have that  connection we still have to interact  with them  so it does take a little bit longer and  but  you know as long as it you'll get to  where you need to go  then it should be fine i think it takes  such  a intricately woven  art to navigate divorce with children  and how we talk to those children and  how  we work with our exes in front of them  or to them how are you dealing with that  part  it was difficult in the beginning  because my emotions and my feelings were  so strong  but i had to keep thinking to myself  especially from  advice from family and friends that keep  your children  the number one priority what is best for  them and that's what you should  do not to say that you have to forget  about  your feelings but just keep them number  one  make sure what they see is positivity  and that no matter what the differences  are  and we do have differences you know  co-parenting difficulties  that we have disagreements about  a lot of things for example education  you know i  i'm a big believer in sending my kids to  catholic school where  he isn't so there's one disagreement but  we have to act as adults and he and i  have to be very mature and just  kind of do that on the side and it's  almost like putting up a show and my  kids are probably too young to even  understand what i'm saying right now but  you're kind of putting  putting a front you know in front of  them just to  make sure that they're seeing the  positive vibes going on  i know that this is so hard but i think  you're  at an amazing place a really  inspirational place  that i'm sure took years and really hard  work to get to  yes that i could definitely agree to and  i  take a lot of my strength from the women  who i know  are with me on this because i know there  are women out there who  feel the same way as i do and i know  that i have a team backing me up  just like you i know you're behind me  and i'm behind you all the way and we  support each other so i take a lot of my  strength  from the other women around me and that  and the other women who i know are going  through the same thing  [Music]  you

